I've got a better suggestion.  Take along a tinning kit.  The tinning
process makes both rotted and poisonous meat safely edible, and you can 
save the tins for later if you're full.  Yes, you can get intrinsics from 
tinned meat...  One nice thing about Archeologists is that they start 
with a tinning kit, and can thus eat anything safely.  (If it's poisonous,
tin it until you get the "you feel healthy" message.)  Kinda makes up for
the crappy armor and weapon.

